  "script": "Apple just made your next Mac mini fifty percent more expensive.\n\nTwice, in under a year.\n\nSo in June, the base price jumped from $599 to $699. Wednesday, it jumped again, to $899.\n\nThat's because of the memory shortage hitting every chipmaker, and Apple just passed that cost straight to you.\n\nNow, here's what your money's actually buying.\n\nHere's the headline: the new M6 is Apple's first chip built on 2 nanometers.\n\nOn top of that, 12 CPU cores, 12 GPU cores, and up to 4 times the AI performance of the M4. Graphics: twice as fast. CPU: 40 percent faster.\n\nWant more? Step up to M5 Pro and you get 18 CPU cores, 20 GPU cores, up to 64 gigs of memory, and Thunderbolt 5.\n\nThat's another $300 jump from last generation, same story.\n\nBut at the new higher price, your storage is still just 256 gigs on the base model.\n\nMeanwhile, pre-orders are open now. It ships to you September 22nd.\n\nAnyways, so is the extra money worth it? The mini's never been this fast. It's also never been this expensive.",
